WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.037 line:0%
-I'm sorry I slept
with your agent.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:07.139 line:0%
-Sorry that --
-And your manager.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.842 line:0%
And your divorce lawyer.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:09.975
-Yeah.

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:14.313
-Uh, I'm sorry I gave up on us.

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:15.981
-Why is it always so hard?

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:17.317
-[ Sighs ]

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.218
I think 'cause you're so strong.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.853
You're so intimidating.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:22.255
You're so talented.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.656
-Hmm.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:28.127
I feel like nobody would be able
to fix the script the way you do

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:32.865
and stay
in such incredible shape.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:37.303
-And you are an amazing mother.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.805
-[ Sighs ]

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:39.973
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.374
We're here with Leslie Mann.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.408
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.977
That was a clip from
"The Bubble."

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.311
-Yes.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:49.915
-So, very COVID-inspired film
about making a film --

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:53.252
an action film with special
effects during COVID.

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.522
So, you have a cast full of
actors, you have a director,

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:58.524
all staying in a luxury hotel
together.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:00:59.959
-Mm-Hmm.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.061
-It also seems like it would be
fun to make

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.164
because that was basically what
you were doing...

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.798
-What was happening, yeah.
-...as well, in real life, too.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:06.999
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, it was.

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:09.368
-And David Duchovny plays
your co-star in the film,

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:12.305
who is also your ex-husband, to
give some context to the clip.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.207
And David Duchovny is a lot
of fun to be around.

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:18.244
-David Duchovny is a lot of fun
to be around, yes.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.012
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:24.050
He is. I mean, he's --

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.653
I've actually known him --
well, I met him,

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:34.928
like, 27 years ago, on
my first job, called "Birdland."

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.029
And he was working on
"The X-Files."

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:43.603
And, um, we met, and I think
he was, like, into me.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.604
-Yeah.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.772
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.275
-And we -- you know,
he invited me to his set,

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:55.380
and then I invited him
to my hotel room

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.350
for a Halloween party.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.986
And then my best friend
and I and David,

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:05.725
with the three of us, were going
to a bar after the party.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.661
And we got into a cab,
started to leave,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:14.400
and David stopped the cab,
and he got out of the cab

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.169
and left the cab.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.170
-Okay.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.738
-Ran away from the cab.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.607
And then didn't speak to me
again for 27 years.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.509
-Really?
-Yes.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:24.844
-Wow!
-I know.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.113
-Did you find out
what you had done?

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:31.317
-So, we talked about it a lot
over the course of 27 years.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.619
Like, "What happened?
What is this?"

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:38.858
And then when we, you know, met
again, or were about to have

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:42.962
this reunion on "The Bubble,"
I like, worked up the courage

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:46.266
to go and ask him,
"What the hell happened?"

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.967
Like, "Why did you get out of
the cab?"

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:53.305
And he said, um, "Oh, yeah,
I kind of remember that.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:55.742
I think I just left my weed
in my room."

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.409
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:59.512
And that was it.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.981
-27 years, you're beating
yourself up --

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.616
-Tortured.
-Just because David Duchovny

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.551
can't remember his weed
before a party.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.787
-Exactly, I know.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.288
-It's very kind that
you forgave him for that.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.923
-Right? Don't do drugs.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:13.525
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:15.695
-Unless you can meet God.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.129
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:20.399
So, you --
there's some roller skating.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.633
You're on roller skates
in this film.

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:22.935
-I am.
-You seem like you know

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.337
what you're doing.
Is this something you learned

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.638
from the film?
-Yeah.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.240
I mean, we all roller skated
when we were kids, right?

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.774
And then we give it up.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:31.644
Like, we give up roller skating
and skateboarding

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:34.480
'cause it's just weird to do
that as an adult, right?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.849
-Yeah, and there's just too high
a risk -- the reward --

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.050
-It's high-Risk, right.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.218
-The reward is not good enough
for the risk.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:43.155
-Right, right, right.
So I picked it up again,

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.690
like, a couple of years ago --

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.160
a year and a half ago,
during lockdown --

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:51.063
and it was just, like,
a good exercise and, like,

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:55.134
a good outlet, you know, for all
of my pent-up energy.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.468
[ Laughs ]

00:03:56.468 --> 00:03:58.304
-Were you roller skating, like,
in the neighborhood?

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.474
-No, I had, like, a little space
this big,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:04.544
and I would just sit in front
of a mirror and like --

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.846
And just go.
And I would watch --

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.981
-You're doing fine
as an empty-nester.

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:10.215
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.215 --> 00:04:12.385
Don't let anybody tell you
you're not thriving.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.421
What with your little at-home
roller skate rink.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.423
[ Laughter ]
-It's so bad.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.824
It's really bad.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:20.359
-Well, at least you're not
talking to cats.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.828
Oh, wait.
-Oh, wait.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:22.828
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:24.930
-Maude gave you her cats?

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.301
-Maude -- okay, so, we have
two cats, Honey and Pumpkin.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:31.570
And then Maude got
two more cats,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.072
Chris, named after Christopher
from "The Sopranos," and Dolly,

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:38.343
and then she dropped them off
at our house

00:04:38.343 --> 00:04:39.945
and never picked them up.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.447
So now we have four cats,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:44.250
and I spend a lot of time
with the cats.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.884
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:49.388
And so, yeah, you know,
the kids notice

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:54.426
that I'm having, like, very long
conversations now with the cats.

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:57.830
And it's gotten a little weird,
but they're great cats.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.266
They're not, like,
your average cat.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.767
They're, like, smart and fun.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:02.901
-They're, like, good listeners.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.037
-They're good listeners.
They are. They're great.

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:06.806
-So, you have a video
of your cat.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.941
Is this --
Who made the video for you?

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.810
-What? Well Honey
made the video.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.211
-Oh, your cat made the video?

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.714
So this would be proof that
this is not your normal cat.

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.549
Let's take a look at Honey
real quick.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.951
-Of course, Leslie and I talk,
Seth.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.819
We're both fascinating people
with a lot to say.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:23.856
What do you expect?

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.792
Don't listen to the haters,
babe.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:29.962
I'm sick of dog people giving us
a hard time.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.097
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.266
-Are you sure you didn't do
ayahuasca?

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:36.302
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.637
-Oh, my God!

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:39.872
See?

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:45.711
They're not like
your average cats. [ Laughs ]

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.346
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:49.248
By the way, Judd's gonna be here
tomorrow.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.616
He wrote a new book.
Have you read it?

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.084
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:54.453
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:56.455
-That's very --
-It's good, yeah.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:06:02.394
This is a good book.
It's about -- he's really into,

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:09.068
like, cartoons since he was
a kid, and -- yeah, it's, um --

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.270
-You're looking at it like
you're hoping to get information

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.338
from the cover.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:15.375
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.544
That's great. That's great.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:19.945
-Yeah, okay.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.646
-Thank you.
What a great --

00:06:21.646 --> 00:06:23.148
What a great sales pitch.

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:25.251
-Leslie Mann, everybody!

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.552
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.554
"The Bubble" is streaming now
on Netflix.

